WEBVTT

00:01:23.880 --> 00:01:26.470
Yeah, yeah, yeah! Things’ve gotten <i>really</i> interesting now!

00:01:26.470 --> 00:01:29.190
These boxing match-ups will be perfect!

00:01:29.970 --> 00:01:33.520
Of course, my favorite to win is cell block six, because Bro Joe is in it!

00:01:33.520 --> 00:01:36.150
That’s what I’ve been wanting to hear!

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:40.380
But then again, there’s that annoying Rikiishi in cell block one!

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:42.760
What about that weakling, Aoyama? What block is he in?

00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:46.650
He's in cell block seven, but he doesn't stand a chance when it comes to physical strength.

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:48.810
The results are about to come in, right?

00:01:48.810 --> 00:01:49.990
Yeah, it’s almost time.

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:52.070
Hey! Looks like you’re having a fun time there, kid.

00:01:52.070 --> 00:01:55.660
Where is this so-called "boxing match" happening?

00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:57.370
I guess I could go. I've got time to kill.

00:01:57.370 --> 00:02:00.090
Um, well, that is... you see...

00:02:00.740 --> 00:02:04.480
It's happening at the Toko Juvenile Prison on Nogiku Island...

00:02:04.480 --> 00:02:06.700
What? At a juvenile prison, you say?

00:02:08.020 --> 00:02:10.220
Don’t laugh! Why is that so funny?

00:02:10.220 --> 00:02:12.030
If you don’t believe us, then go see for yourself!

00:02:12.030 --> 00:02:15.370
Hey! I thought I told you punks to stop scribbling on people's walls!

00:02:17.140 --> 00:02:18.510
That was a close one!

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:20.970
That old guy really gives me the willies.

00:02:20.970 --> 00:02:21.880
Me too.

00:02:22.550 --> 00:02:23.550
It’s the old man!

00:02:23.550 --> 00:02:26.570
Hey, guys, the old man is back! Back from the fight!

00:02:27.420 --> 00:02:30.020
Hey, old man!

00:02:30.020 --> 00:02:31.990
How’s Bro Joe?

00:02:30.270 --> 00:02:31.990
<i>How did it go?</i>

00:02:32.370 --> 00:02:34.040
Don’t tell me he <i>lost</i>?

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:35.090
Old man!

00:02:35.090 --> 00:02:36.390
Tell us what happened, old man!

00:02:36.390 --> 00:02:37.930
He won.

00:02:37.930 --> 00:02:39.000
All right!

00:02:39.000 --> 00:02:40.180
He won!

00:02:40.180 --> 00:02:42.650
But he won without honor.

00:02:43.990 --> 00:02:46.020
<i>Hey! That's dirty, Yabuki!</i>

00:02:45.070 --> 00:02:46.020
<i>What do you think you're doing!?</i>

00:02:52.600 --> 00:02:55.510
<i>Foul! Minus one point!</i>

00:02:55.510 --> 00:02:56.250
<i>Shut up!</i>

00:02:57.710 --> 00:03:01.070
<i>Take off as many as you like!</i>

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:39.820
<i>Hey! See that? Look at Matsuki's feet!</i>

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:41.650
<i>W-What the...</i>

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:43.320
<i>Matsuki's feet are floating.</i>

00:03:47.740 --> 00:03:49.620
<i>That’s what he gets for taking on Joe!</i>

00:03:49.620 --> 00:03:51.440
<i>That bastard is beating him to a pulp!</i>

00:04:38.720 --> 00:04:42.950
<i>Well, time for you to raise my arm and show these bastards who won, Mr. Referee.</i>

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:47.460
<i>Why not?</i>

00:04:57.790 --> 00:05:02.480
<i>In terms of your technique and etiquette, this was a horrible match.</i>

00:05:06.970 --> 00:05:09.290
<i>What the hell!? Come back here, you old fart!</i>

00:05:09.290 --> 00:05:10.400
<i>Whaddaya mean, "etiquette"?</i>

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:11.600
<i>Whaddaya mean, "horrible"?</i>

00:05:11.600 --> 00:05:15.300
<i>Heh! Since when was boxing such a classy affair?</i>

00:05:15.300 --> 00:05:18.150
<i>Lemme tell ya what boxing is all about. Winning! That's all that matters!</i>

00:05:19.770 --> 00:05:22.250
<i>I guess ya get it after all, Joe.</i>

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:23.190
<i>You’re right.</i>

00:05:23.190 --> 00:05:24.890
<i>If you win, good for you.</i>

00:05:24.890 --> 00:05:27.800
<i>But I wonder... can you defeat Aoyama?</i>

00:05:27.800 --> 00:05:30.050
<i>What? Of course!</i>

00:05:30.050 --> 00:05:31.770
<i>You really think that weakling can beat me?</i>

00:05:31.770 --> 00:05:36.820
<i>Listen, old man, next Sunday, bring your beloved protégé with you!</i>

00:05:36.820 --> 00:05:39.120
<i>Don't you dare praise him after I've beaten his face to a pulp!</i>

00:05:42.430 --> 00:05:45.600
With that rotten attitude, he doesn't stand a chance.

00:05:45.600 --> 00:05:49.340
Eh, what did you say? No way, old man!

00:05:49.340 --> 00:05:52.480
Since when did you take on that stupid Aoyama as your protégé?

00:05:52.480 --> 00:05:54.090
Did you fire Joe?

00:05:54.090 --> 00:05:56.700
Hey, old fart! We're not leaving until we get an answer!

00:05:56.700 --> 00:05:57.070
Yeah!

00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:59.090
Be good little kids, now and piss off.

00:05:57.450 --> 00:06:00.340
<i>Hey! Get back here, old man!</i>

00:06:01.590 --> 00:06:04.110
Dammit! Hinako, get me a match!

00:06:04.110 --> 00:06:07.590
Uh... by "match" you mean that thing that makes fire, like this?

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:10.980
I’m gonna burn that old man's house down!

00:06:10.980 --> 00:06:12.490
Sachi! Don’t be so rash!

00:06:12.490 --> 00:06:13.800
Please don’t do it, Sachi!

00:06:13.800 --> 00:06:16.380
But... I just can’t stand it.

00:06:16.380 --> 00:06:19.790
I hate seeing Bro Joe so alone.

00:06:22.520 --> 00:06:24.070
Bro Joe <i>won</i> the match!

00:06:26.070 --> 00:06:28.570
No matter what anyone else says, he <i>won</i>!

00:06:30.680 --> 00:06:32.070
And he’s not gonna lose either!

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:34.790
Hey, Sachi, you can’t stay out here forever.

00:06:34.790 --> 00:06:36.980
It's getting late.

00:06:38.040 --> 00:06:41.050
He’s not gonna lose to that idiotic Aoyama!

00:06:44.260 --> 00:06:47.860
Who are you gonna bet on in the next match?

00:06:47.860 --> 00:06:50.760
Just take a look at the fighters and you'll see who's gonna win.

00:06:58.410 --> 00:06:59.430
Hey, check it out.

00:06:59.430 --> 00:07:02.060
It looks like he’s gotten much stronger.

00:07:02.060 --> 00:07:03.430
I’m talking about Aoyama.

00:07:03.430 --> 00:07:05.600
I wonder how Joe compares now.

00:07:07.580 --> 00:07:11.400
I think Aoyama's defensive technique is going to cut off Joe's attack.

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:12.800
Jackass!

00:07:12.800 --> 00:07:15.760
Have ya forgotten about that punch of Joe’s?

00:07:15.760 --> 00:07:18.700
He punched that guy off his feet and out of the ring!

00:07:18.700 --> 00:07:19.830
Dammit!

00:07:21.370 --> 00:07:24.420
Looks like your punch is amazing, too.

00:07:25.190 --> 00:07:27.810
So I guess Joe’s killer punch is king, eh?

00:07:27.810 --> 00:07:29.890
Joe’s punch...

00:07:29.890 --> 00:07:32.890
I think its real power is that when you’re up against it, you lose your nerve.

00:07:32.890 --> 00:07:37.990
Maybe you're right. If he loses to Aoyama, it will prove he's been a slacker the whole time.

00:07:35.390 --> 00:07:37.990
<i>I don’t even care anymore! I just want a fight, dammit!</i>

00:07:39.780 --> 00:07:41.930
Today's the deadline to place your bets.

00:07:41.930 --> 00:07:44.440
Aoyama or Joe... hell if I know who'll win.

00:07:44.860 --> 00:07:47.390
Why don't we ask Rikiishi what he thinks?

00:07:58.660 --> 00:08:00.950
You guys up to that monkey business again?

00:08:01.770 --> 00:08:03.800
Hey, this is serious.

00:08:03.800 --> 00:08:06.580
I don't know who’s going to win, but I'll say this:

00:08:06.580 --> 00:08:10.060
The bottomless power of martial arts will be revealed to you quite clearly.

00:08:10.060 --> 00:08:14.690
Um, could you be a <i>little</i> more specific?

00:08:14.690 --> 00:08:18.470
The answer lies with that eye-patched old man.

00:08:34.690 --> 00:08:37.200
Lower those hips! Loosen up your core!

00:08:37.770 --> 00:08:40.190
Looks as though they're all fired up.

00:08:40.190 --> 00:08:42.210
Listen to him wheeze! Hear that?

00:08:43.180 --> 00:08:45.470
Guess Joe isn't such a safe bet after all.

00:08:45.470 --> 00:08:48.440
I saw it! The real "bottomless power of martial arts."

00:08:48.440 --> 00:08:50.820
I think he meant Aoyama has a secret advantage.

00:08:50.820 --> 00:08:53.210
I guess Joe winning would be too obvious.

00:08:53.210 --> 00:08:56.800
Well, just to be safe, let’s go see what Joe is up to.

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:58.070
Let’s go.

00:08:58.070 --> 00:09:00.300
I feel like I'm going to a horsetrack.

00:09:01.900 --> 00:09:05.070
Apparently, Aoyama is in no condition to train because his feet are busted.

00:09:05.070 --> 00:09:08.770
He's going to get clobbered if he keeps underestimating his opponent.

00:09:08.770 --> 00:09:11.240
He's really gonna be a bloody mess.

00:09:14.790 --> 00:09:16.140
All right, I've decided!

00:09:16.140 --> 00:09:18.540
I bet ten days' breakfast on Aoyama!

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:19.390
Me too!

00:09:19.390 --> 00:09:21.010
I bet a supply voucher on Aoyama.

00:09:21.010 --> 00:09:22.340
I bet five days worth of dinner.

00:09:22.340 --> 00:09:25.060
Easy, guys. If we all bet on Aoyama, then it's not much of a bet.

00:09:25.060 --> 00:09:27.080
What's with that half-hearted attitude?

00:09:27.080 --> 00:09:29.150
He’s like a kid cying over being called a mama's boy.

00:09:29.150 --> 00:09:31.500
Everyone in the world is betting on Aoyama.

00:09:31.500 --> 00:09:34.220
If no one’s put a bet in for Joe, this means there's no point in betting anymore.

00:09:34.220 --> 00:09:37.360
Okay! Then I’ll put in a bet for Joe and clean up!

00:09:37.360 --> 00:09:40.450
If I win, I'll be able to eat all the food I want,

00:09:40.450 --> 00:09:43.880
and I can wear countless pairs of clean underpants every day!

00:09:44.550 --> 00:09:49.000
Sure, but if Joe <i>doesn't</i> win, you won’t get any food <i>or</i> underpants.

00:09:49.000 --> 00:09:51.630
No underpants, eh? That’s a bit harsh.

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:25.270
Pick up those heels!

00:10:25.850 --> 00:10:27.300
And breathe through your nose, not your mouth.

00:10:27.300 --> 00:10:28.320
Yes, Sir!

00:10:31.720 --> 00:10:33.270
Go! Oh, wait a minute.

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:34.850
Your shoe is untied.

00:10:35.470 --> 00:10:36.770
Thank you, Sir.

00:10:41.460 --> 00:10:44.190
Well then, before the sun sets, let’s run another lap.

00:10:44.190 --> 00:10:45.150
Yes, Sir!

00:10:45.150 --> 00:10:45.910
Go!

00:11:49.960 --> 00:11:50.770
Shit...

00:11:55.500 --> 00:11:56.780
Old man...

00:11:57.150 --> 00:11:59.090
What the hell are you trying to do?

00:11:59.090 --> 00:12:02.770
What’s your logic? Why are you pushing me into a corner?

00:12:06.430 --> 00:12:10.200
No matter what, I’m gonna win tomorrow. 
I’m gonna thoroughly beat Aoyama to a pulp.

00:12:10.200 --> 00:12:11.040
Old man...

00:12:15.850 --> 00:12:19.420
I'm gonna make Aoyama pay for your betrayal.

00:12:19.420 --> 00:12:21.510
I’m gonna do it! I’m gonna do it!

00:12:21.510 --> 00:12:25.090
I’m gonna do it! I’m gonna do it!

00:12:42.440 --> 00:12:43.640
Big news, Chief!

00:12:43.640 --> 00:12:44.990
What’s all the ruckus about?

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:46.990
Shiraki Yohko-san just came in the helicopter.

00:12:47.540 --> 00:12:50.950
But Yohko-san always comes to see the boxing matches.

00:12:50.950 --> 00:12:52.080
Yes, but...

00:12:52.810 --> 00:12:55.460
Today she’s brought along her grandfather, Mikinosuke.

00:12:55.460 --> 00:12:57.910
A-Are you sure?

00:12:57.910 --> 00:12:59.960
Shiraki Mikinosuke... At a place like this...

00:13:00.430 --> 00:13:02.920
Calling all personnel! Form the formal formation immediately!

00:13:14.660 --> 00:13:15.730
Wow!

00:13:15.730 --> 00:13:18.270
What a welcoming party!

00:13:19.690 --> 00:13:22.430
Give a warm greeting to Shiraki Mikinosuke-sensei.

00:13:22.430 --> 00:13:23.620
Bow!

00:13:25.490 --> 00:13:27.730
You call that bowing?

00:13:29.490 --> 00:13:31.250
Ah, thank you, thank you.

00:13:31.760 --> 00:13:33.890
Good work, good work.

00:13:33.890 --> 00:13:39.230
We cannot thank you enough for the boxing equipment and funding you've given us.

00:13:39.230 --> 00:13:41.210
Please accept our gratitude.

00:13:41.210 --> 00:13:43.020
Thank you very much, Sir!

00:13:43.020 --> 00:13:46.220
Oh, I’m flattered, but let’s dispose of all this stuffy formality.

00:13:47.270 --> 00:13:48.720
I apologize, Sir.

00:13:48.720 --> 00:13:54.800
It’s nothing. I only came here because my granddaughter wanted to watch a match with me.

00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:57.150
However, I've developed an interest in the boxing program you've set up here.

00:13:57.150 --> 00:13:59.730
You see, boxing has always been a passion of mine.

00:14:00.400 --> 00:14:03.740
Grandfather, I think you’ll be happy you came to see this match.

00:14:03.740 --> 00:14:07.550
I assure you, you'll see amazing boxing that rivals even professional matches. {Das: Needs to be broken up.}

00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:13.420
Well, please come in. We have a special seat prepared for you.

00:14:13.420 --> 00:14:14.210
Thank you.

00:14:20.200 --> 00:14:23.170
Amazing boxing like in professional matches?

00:14:23.170 --> 00:14:24.480
She must mean Aoyama and me.

00:14:24.480 --> 00:14:26.720
Damn that pushy woman.

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:29.420
Just what kind of match does she think will happen to make it so "amazing"?

00:14:29.420 --> 00:14:30.020
Joe!

00:14:31.490 --> 00:14:36.360
Listen... You won’t lose, even though you’re all alone now, right?

00:14:36.360 --> 00:14:37.360
You’re strong, right?

00:14:37.360 --> 00:14:38.640
You talkin’ to me?

00:14:38.640 --> 00:14:40.190
Cut it out!

00:14:40.190 --> 00:14:43.070
Well I’m here to cheer ya on at least! As a representative!

00:14:43.070 --> 00:14:46.860
I couldn't get the rest of my friends on the helicopter,

00:14:46.860 --> 00:14:51.200
but I will make sure to get a photo of all the best parts of the match... like this!

00:14:53.140 --> 00:14:54.500
We haven’t seen each other in a long time!

00:14:54.500 --> 00:14:56.210
I'm really excited to see you again, even if you're not.

00:14:58.930 --> 00:15:01.170
Hey! Challenger, over there!

00:15:02.080 --> 00:15:05.160
Go get dressed and get in the ring already!

00:15:21.190 --> 00:15:27.180
Hey! Whaddaya mean, "Challenger"! He’s got a name. He's Yabuki Joe!

00:15:27.180 --> 00:15:29.970
Tell ‘em off for treating you like that, Joe!

00:15:29.970 --> 00:15:32.800
Geez, you stupid old man!

00:15:32.800 --> 00:15:35.040
Um... yeah.

00:15:47.710 --> 00:15:49.470
What’s wrong, old man?

00:15:49.470 --> 00:15:54.250
That look on your face says, "I want everyone to see just how strong my beloved protégé is."

00:15:54.250 --> 00:15:56.860
It sounds like this is the match of your dreams.

00:15:57.620 --> 00:15:58.540
Hey, Yabuki!

00:15:58.540 --> 00:16:01.260
Unlike <i>you</i>, Aoyama is really excited about fighting!

00:16:01.260 --> 00:16:03.620
Stop pretending he doesn't frighten you!

00:16:03.620 --> 00:16:05.440
Are ya too scared to get into the ring?

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:07.600
Nishi! Where's Nishi!?

00:16:07.600 --> 00:16:10.070
You're supposed to have my gear, Nishi!

00:16:10.070 --> 00:16:11.910
Move it! Where is he!?

00:16:14.940 --> 00:16:17.370
Jackass, I ain’t an octopus.

00:16:17.920 --> 00:16:19.240
Just give me the biggest gloves you have!

00:16:21.860 --> 00:16:23.670
Shit, you really are useless, aren't ya?

00:16:24.990 --> 00:16:27.170
Here. It’s your mouth piece. Take it.

00:16:27.730 --> 00:16:30.170
Mouth piece? I don’t need that.

00:16:30.670 --> 00:16:34.170
Don’t be crazy! You’ll cut your mouth open right away.

00:16:34.170 --> 00:16:37.550
Mind your own business. You think I'm stupid enough to let my mouth get cut?

00:16:41.050 --> 00:16:42.660
Oh, he's so cool!

00:16:45.910 --> 00:16:47.940
Yo! Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:16:47.940 --> 00:16:50.560
You can ring that bell whenever you want.

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:53.510
Before that, I have a briefing for you.

00:16:53.510 --> 00:16:54.570
Come to the center of the ring.

00:16:59.490 --> 00:17:02.370
What the hell? What’s with that guy’s attitude?

00:17:02.370 --> 00:17:05.680
Just when we thought he’d started to behave, he pulls this stunt.

00:17:03.890 --> 00:17:08.200
<i>Once I ring the bell, you must return to your neutral corners.</i>

00:17:08.200 --> 00:17:09.050
Do you get it?

00:17:10.760 --> 00:17:14.420
Stupid Joe! What a disgrace!

00:17:14.420 --> 00:17:16.050
Don’t worry, don’t worry.

00:17:16.470 --> 00:17:19.550
Bro Joe! Good luck!

00:17:20.150 --> 00:17:21.550
All right! Leave it to me!

00:17:22.000 --> 00:17:25.850
He knows by now just how powerful Aoyama can be, but he still acts so cocky?

00:17:25.850 --> 00:17:27.270
I swear, "Bluff" must be his middle name.

00:17:28.160 --> 00:17:31.230
I wouldn't say it's {/i1}all{/i0} a bluff.

00:17:31.230 --> 00:17:32.740
Why not, Grandfather?

00:17:33.910 --> 00:17:36.400
Even though he knows what he’s up against, he still acts like the situation is under control.

00:17:36.400 --> 00:17:38.930
Some would call that "determination."

00:17:38.930 --> 00:17:43.600
He knows that if he loses the match after putting on such a show, he’ll be very embarrassed.

00:17:43.600 --> 00:17:46.630
In order to avoid that embarrassment, he must fight the fight of his life.

00:17:46.630 --> 00:17:49.250
In other words, he’s purposely backed himself into a corner.

00:17:49.250 --> 00:17:51.800
I think he might be consciously planning it.

00:17:54.760 --> 00:17:56.310
Are ya ready yet!?

00:17:56.310 --> 00:17:57.780
We’re getting bored!

00:17:57.780 --> 00:17:58.760
Just fight already!

00:17:58.760 --> 00:18:01.600
I don’t care what anyone else says, you can do it!

00:17:58.760 --> 00:18:00.290
<i>Get him, Aoyama!</i>

00:18:01.600 --> 00:18:03.890
Beat that idiot down!

00:18:03.290 --> 00:18:05.850
<i>Understood? Now return to your corners.</i>

00:18:05.850 --> 00:18:07.270
Not so fast, Aoyama.

00:18:08.040 --> 00:18:11.280
I hope you don't get knocked out too soon and make your sweet old man cry.

00:18:12.780 --> 00:18:13.280
Thank you!

00:18:14.180 --> 00:18:18.280
You, too. I hope you don't get knocked out too soon and make everyone too happy.

00:18:18.280 --> 00:18:19.280
That was awesome!

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:20.990
You already got a point taken away, Joe!

00:18:23.120 --> 00:18:25.590
Hey, what did you just say, Aoyama!?

00:18:26.450 --> 00:18:30.750
Just take it easy, Yabuki-san. The bell will ring soon, but until then, let’s be friends.

00:18:30.750 --> 00:18:33.750
And another blow for Joe! That was smooth!

00:18:36.090 --> 00:18:38.760
Dammit all! Joe! Do something!

00:18:39.290 --> 00:18:43.780
Yo, Ao. Just because some old guy gave you lessons, doesn’t mean you’re allowed to talk to me like that.

00:18:43.780 --> 00:18:46.320
Even if you beg on your hands and knees, I’ll still show you no mercy!

00:18:46.320 --> 00:18:47.520
That’s a penalty.

00:18:48.750 --> 00:18:49.960
Penalty?

00:18:49.960 --> 00:18:51.950
"Unnecessary rough language in the ring,

00:18:51.950 --> 00:18:56.510
in an attempt to lower the guard of one’s opponent before a match, results in a penalty for the guilty party."

00:18:56.510 --> 00:18:58.020
You get it, right?

00:18:58.020 --> 00:18:59.590
Hey, hey, you stupid old man!

00:18:59.590 --> 00:19:02.640
Are you gonna nitpick over the rules just so Aoyama can win?

00:19:04.590 --> 00:19:06.160
You really prefer him over me?

00:19:06.160 --> 00:19:07.650
You really hate me that much?

00:19:07.650 --> 00:19:10.090
And yet another point deduction.

00:19:11.630 --> 00:19:15.520
"Abuse against the referee" is an even bigger offense.

00:19:15.520 --> 00:19:17.790
Penalty for that violation can go as far as automatic disqualification.

00:19:19.040 --> 00:19:19.800
Why you...

00:19:20.510 --> 00:19:22.580
What’s with that attitude?

00:19:22.580 --> 00:19:24.310
You wanna lose by disqualification?

00:19:26.760 --> 00:19:27.960
Disqualification, eh?

00:19:29.320 --> 00:19:32.310
I don’t want that. I can’t have that.

00:19:32.310 --> 00:19:33.570
Old man...

00:19:33.570 --> 00:19:36.060
No, "Mr. Referee."

00:19:36.060 --> 00:19:40.320
I'm not giving up till you've seen Aoyama's face ruined by my fists.

00:19:41.030 --> 00:19:42.660
That was really stupid.

00:19:42.660 --> 00:19:47.290
This is only the third round of matches and you've already got two point deductions!

00:19:47.940 --> 00:19:49.550
Two points is nothing to get worried about!

00:19:49.550 --> 00:19:52.910
Even if I took <i>ten</i> point deductions, I still just need one killer punch to win the match!

00:19:52.910 --> 00:19:53.790
Joe! Behind you!

00:19:58.840 --> 00:20:00.180
Joe!

00:19:59.080 --> 00:20:00.180
<i>Joe! Joe!</i>

00:20:00.720 --> 00:20:01.780
He’s pretty good.

00:20:01.780 --> 00:20:03.180
Punching him from the very start!

00:20:12.390 --> 00:20:14.480
Woah, woah, woah...

00:20:19.720 --> 00:20:21.730
A liver blow, I'm very surprised.

00:20:21.730 --> 00:20:25.490
I had no idea a boxing match at a juvenile prison could present this level of technique.

00:20:28.540 --> 00:20:30.180
Hang in there, hang in there!

00:20:30.180 --> 00:20:31.370
Hang in there, Joe!

00:20:31.370 --> 00:20:32.610
I'm sick of this!

00:20:35.050 --> 00:20:36.270
The "hit-and-run" strategy.

00:20:36.270 --> 00:20:38.730
He attacks, then withdraws, then repeats that dance.

00:20:38.730 --> 00:20:40.000
Yet another first-class technique.

00:20:46.470 --> 00:20:48.870
Joe’s mouth is all bloody!

00:20:48.870 --> 00:20:50.920
Ao's punches aren't dull anymore.

00:20:50.920 --> 00:20:52.980
They're as sharp as blades now.

00:20:52.980 --> 00:20:56.480
Joe! What’s wrong with you!? Get him!

00:20:54.710 --> 00:20:56.490
<i>Joe! What's going on!?</i>

00:20:59.620 --> 00:21:02.560
Aoyama's plan is to attack and not give up an inch.

00:21:02.560 --> 00:21:04.980
We have a real match here.

00:21:07.700 --> 00:21:09.450
What's wrong, you two?

00:21:09.450 --> 00:21:11.270
Ao! Don’t let him recover!

00:21:11.270 --> 00:21:12.250
Hit him! Hit him!

00:21:12.250 --> 00:21:13.760
Deliver the final blow, Aoyama!

00:21:13.760 --> 00:21:16.450
Joe's a pushover!

00:21:17.010 --> 00:21:17.960
Fight!

00:21:38.710 --> 00:21:41.000
What the hell are you swinging at?

00:21:41.000 --> 00:21:43.620
This is no time to Go-Go dance!

00:21:49.530 --> 00:21:51.950
He advances, hits, then withdraws.

00:21:51.950 --> 00:21:55.050
Looks like I've gotta rethink this.

00:21:55.050 --> 00:21:59.500
We'll see who's worthy of learning the legendary techniques of the Tange Danpei era.

00:22:03.280 --> 00:22:05.650
Shit... You think you’re so hot...

00:22:24.350 --> 00:22:26.110
He's down! Go to a neutral corner.

00:22:26.530 --> 00:22:27.560
1!

00:22:27.560 --> 00:22:28.550
I'm down, am I?

00:22:28.550 --> 00:22:30.270
2!

00:22:30.270 --> 00:22:32.580
3!

00:22:30.750 --> 00:22:32.580
I’m not down; I just slipped.

00:22:32.580 --> 00:22:34.340
4!

00:22:34.340 --> 00:22:35.620
5!

00:22:36.170 --> 00:22:37.240
I slipped!

00:22:37.240 --> 00:22:39.130
You were down, Joe.

00:22:39.130 --> 00:22:40.750
Can’t ya stop the damn count, then!?

00:22:40.750 --> 00:22:42.920
In the ring, talking back is a penalty.

00:22:42.920 --> 00:22:45.300
If you keep this up, you'll lose by disqualification.

00:22:49.880 --> 00:22:51.220
Fight!

00:23:15.470 --> 00:23:19.510
Am I going to lose... to that weakling, Aoyama?

00:23:19.510 --> 00:23:22.230
And the old man...

00:23:22.230 --> 00:23:26.320
Why... Why... Why...

00:23:26.320 --> 00:23:28.630
Why do I have to lose?

00:23:28.630 --> 00:23:29.470
Why me?

00:23:30.420 --> 00:23:31.660
Why?

00:24:43.720 --> 00:24:46.520
The match between Joe and Aoyama is raging!

00:24:46.520 --> 00:24:49.320
After Aoyama took the lead, Joe went down for the count.

00:24:49.320 --> 00:24:53.210
And then... at the end of the count, Joe stood again.

00:24:53.210 --> 00:24:57.300
So, with Joe covered in battle scars, which way is tomorrow!?
